data: {"type":"TOOL_CALL_RESULT","toolCallId":"call_178bb0f5eb82408aa2fe5a7a","messageId":"5ccc4395-e5f7-4785-82f1-cc8ef44593c5","content":"{\"ok\":true,\"result\":{\"path\":\"/skills/ui-layout/SKILL.md\",\"content\":\"1: ---\\n2: name: ui-layout\\n3: description: Use for Layout Tree decisions involving Row, Column, Stack, Panel, Slot, Sidebar, dimensions, resizing, placement, and composition of existing plugin nodes.\\n4: compatibility: Agent UI Plugin Creator AppUIModel and deterministic compiler boundary.\\n5: allowed-tools: enable_creator_tools read_file ls glob grep inspect_ui_project inspect_app_ui_model inspect_ui_slots list_ui_plugins inspect_ui_plugin mutate_app_ui_model execute\\n6: ---\\n7: \\n8: # UI Layout\\n9: \\n10: Express composition through the AppUIModel Layout Tree rather than DOM manipulation or ad-hoc Plugin CSS.\\n11: \\n12: Do not load this Skill for an eligible `insert_plugin_default` request from a\\n13: fresh Composition Snapshot. The Host resolves the declared authoring placement,\\n14: size, track materialization, and low-level lowering atomically. Load this Skill\\n15: when the semantic operation is unavailable, fails closed, or the user requests\\n16: custom Layout placement or geometry.\\n17: \\n18: ## Node semantics\\n19: \\n20: - `sidebar`: wraps the main `content` and ordered single-plugin navigation `items`.\\n21: - `row`: lays out children horizontally. Optional `sizes` correspond by index to `children`.\\n22: - `column`: lays out children vertically. Optional `sizes` correspond by index to `children`.\\n23: - `stack`: overlays or switches among children; `activeIndex` selects a direct child by index.\\n24: - `panel`: wraps one child and may define width, height, min/max width, or resizing.\\n25: - `slot`: is a physical structural location with an ordered `plugins` array. It has no persisted id, description, hint, or Runtime slot id.\\n26: \\n27: ## Layout rules\\n28: \\n29: - Preserve existing child order and regions unless the request says otherwise.\\n30: - Use the observed `nodeRef` only for the current mutation snapshot. Store each visual plugin directly in the Slot where it appears.\\n31: - For a fixed right region, use a Row with the main content first and a right Panel second.\\n32: - Left/right position and ordering are always Layout Tree changes. Move the existing\\n33:   Plugin instance or its enclosing Panel through `mutate_app_ui_model`; never use\\n34:   `flex-direction`, `order`, transforms or absolute positioning to reverse regions.\\n35:   Move a navigation Panel together with its identity Header and history when the\\n36:   request concerns that whole region. Preserve Plugin identities and child Slots.\\n37: - Platform presets use an explicit Row of navigation/content Panels. Optional\\n38:   left/center/right regions are materialized only when occupied; do not add blank\\n39:   fixed-width columns. Generic Sidebar remains supported for existing layouts.\\n40: - `row.responsive: { type: \\\"drawer\\\", primaryIndex, drawerIndex, minPrimaryWidth }`\\n41:   identifies the main child and the collapsible navigation child. Its drawer opens\\n42:   on the side implied by child order. Moving a Panel preserves those child\\n43:   identities and updates their indices. The legacy `trailing-drawer` policy still\\n44:   requires a drawer after the primary child. When explicitly replacing a Row,\\n45:   declare indices matching the final children.\\n46: - When a Row `sizes` entry and a child Panel `width` describe the same fixed dimension, update both consistently.\\n47: - For Row and Column layouts, the parent `sizes` owns the grid tracks. A fixed-size child Panel does not shrink its parent track. For a fixed sidebar, set the parent tracks to `[W, minmax(0, 1fr)]` and use the matching child Panel width when that authoring constraint is also needed. `gap` only controls space between tracks; inspect the parent tracks and child bounds before attributing a visible layout issue to `gap`.\\n48: - Creator Row/Column track sizes always use explicit CSS strings. Correct values\\n49:   include `\\\"280px\\\"`, `\\\"1fr\\\"`, and `\\\"minmax(0, 1fr)\\\"`; never send numeric\\n50:   track sizes through Creator mutation operations. Runtime numeric Row/Column\\n51:   sizes represent fractional tracks, not pixels. A fixed sidebar example is\\n52:   `[\\\"280px\\\", \\\"minmax(0, 1fr)\\\"]`.\\n53: - When inserting into a Row or Column that already has `sizes`, pass the new\\n54:   child's `size` on `insert_layout_node`, `move_layout_node`, or\\n55:   `insert_layout_relative`; a later `update_layout_node_props` cannot rescue an\\n56:   earlier sequential operation that already failed. When\\n57:   `insert_layout_relative` creates a new sized wrapper, pass `size` and\\n58:   `anchorSize` together.\\n59: - Use a nested Column for vertical subdivision and Stack only when overlapping or active-view behavior is intended.\\n60: - Do not add a plugin node until you have confirmed the referenced Plugin exists.\\n61: - Do not edit Runtime layout code for an application-specific arrangement.\\n62: \\n63: For a pure Layout change, start from\\n64: `inspect_ui_project({\\\"view\\\":\\\"composition\\\"})`; do not re-read AppUIModel,\\n65: manifests, Plugin source, CSS, Services, or generated files when that fresh\\n66: snapshot already contains the needed refs, sizes, Slots, instances, capability\\n67: summaries, authoring placement/size guidance, Service readiness, Host\\n68: guarantees, and constraints. Treat authoring placement and size as defaults:\\n69: explicit user intent and the current Composition take precedence. Apply the\\n70: change through `mutate_app_ui_model` with\\n71: the exact inspected hash. Prefer one batch, use `insert_layout_relative` for\\n72: deterministic left/right/above/below placement, and use `$localRef` when a later\\n73: operation must reference a node created in the same transaction.\\n74: \\n75: ## Generic Sidebar\\n76: \\n77: `sidebar` is a Layout container, not a Plugin. It has `defaultActive: null | itemId`,\\n78: ordered `items: [{ id, child: { type: \\\"slot\\\", plugins: [oneVisualPlugin] } }]`, and\\n79: `content` containing the ordinary Layout Tree. Never store icons, labels or live\\n80: collapse state in AppUIModel. The selected Plugin manifest must declare `sidebar`\\n81: with a supported Lucide icon and optional `en-US`/`zh-CN` labels (Plugin name fallback).\\n82: Supported icons: `messages-square`, `folder`, `folder-open`, `files`, `search`,\\n83: `settings`, `database`, `chart-no-axes-combined`, `list`, `bot`, `book-open`, `star`,\\n84: `circle-help`. Inspect the manifest before choosing a Sidebar placement; edit\\n85: Plugin navigation metadata only when the user asks to change its icon or label.\\n86: \\n87: Use deterministic `mutate_app_ui_model` operations:\\n88: \\n89: - `insert_sidebar_item`: `sidebarRef`, unique `itemId`, optional `index`, and\\n90:   exactly one of `plugin` (new instance) or `instanceId` (move existing instance).\\n91: - `remove_sidebar_item`: `sidebarRef`, `itemId`. Removes its composition entry;\\n92:   preserves Plugin source. Moving out instead uses `move_plugin` to an observed\\n93:   ordinary `layout_slot` or `plugin_slot`; the empty Sidebar item is pruned.\\n94: - `reorder_sidebar_items`: `sidebarRef`, `itemIds` containing every item exactly once.\\n95: - `update_layout_node_props`: `nodeRef`, `set: { defaultActive: null | itemId }`.\\n96: \\n97: These operations participate in the existing atomic transaction and final\\n98: composition validation. For a project without Sidebar, use `replace_layout_node`\\n99: with a complete Sidebar container preserving existing Plugin instances in its\\n100: `content` and moving selected instances into its items. Do not infer tree changes\\n101: from strings or DOM selectors. Desktop rail is 48px with a 280px active panel;\\n102: containers narrower than 648px use a scoped Sheet. Sidebar is available for\\n103: explicit navigation-container composition; preserve existing project layouts.\\n104: \\n105: ### Optional Sidebar Header\\n106: \\n107: `sidebar.header` is an optional ordinary Layout Slot containing at most one visual\\n108: Plugin (zero is valid after removal). It needs no manifest navigation metadata.\\n109: Inspect its existing Slot ref and use `insert_plugin`, `remove_plugin`,\\n110: `replace_plugin`, `move_plugin`, or enable/disable operations just as for any\\n111: Layout Slot. `replace_layout_node` can declare an optional Header Slot, including\\n112: a transaction-local ref; there is no Header-specific install operation.\\n113: \\n114: For Agent name, logo, description or branding requests, reuse `agent-identity`\\n115: and edit `plugins/agent-identity/config.ts`. Its localized defaults use the\\n116: `agentIdentity` namespace; custom brand content need not be translated. Do not\\n117: edit SidebarFrame, vendor components or create a Service to change identity.\\n118: Legacy platform Sidebar presets select history by default; new platform presets\\n119: express navigation as ordinary Row/Panel/Slot composition.\\n120: Models without Header retain the legacy navigation rail. A Header with one\\n121: enabled navigation item uses a single column without a duplicate history icon.\\n122: \",\"hash\":\"a90ae661af2d28b386c251bab64c08fb02fd2257bc1f928f7b525bd014ae070f\",\"totalLines\":122,\"nextOffset\":null}}","role":"tool"}

